[$in title:["Directives"]]
[$in description:["General compiler directives in Moth, including the template-head form, the source-modifier form, configuration, builder slots and shared operand rules."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
[section, $md:
    # Directives

    `$` introduces a registered compiler directive. Template-head directives
    already use this marker. The accepted source-modifier family adds next-construct
    modifiers such as `$config` and later compiler-owned forms. HTML document
    metadata uses direct const inserts in `@entry.moth` through builder slots.

    Template directives are implemented. The `$config` source modifier is
    delivered for typed build inputs; later compiler-owned source forms remain
    accepted design. No root-purpose directive exists: `@entry.moth` owns entry
    eligibility, and `$entry` and `$page` are not source syntax.
]

